msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1414
msgid "Narrowing this drafts products."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1415
msgid "Articles the filter excludes are no longer in the feed, so the next product sync drafts the ones it previously imported. Widening the filter again republishes them."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1422
msgid "Image base URL"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1432
msgid "Kontor returns image filenames rather than URLs. Set the folder they live in to import product images; leave blank to skip images."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1436
msgid "Articles without images"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1455
msgid "Only import articles that Kontor lists an image for"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1458
msgid "An article with no image is passed over rather than created. The check is on what Kontor sends, not on the shop, so a product whose pictures are still downloading is never caught by it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1461
msgid "This drafts products already imported."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1462
msgid "A product this plugin imported whose article now arrives without an image is drafted, exactly as one Kontor stopped listing is. It is republished by itself as soon as the article has an image again, or when this setting is turned off."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1467
msgid "Sales quantities"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1485
msgid "Hold customers to the quantities Kontor sells each article in"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1488
msgid "Kontor states a smallest quantity and a step for every article, imported as _wksync_min_qty and _wksync_qty_step. An article sold in sixes with a step of two can then only be bought as 6, 8, 10 and so on — in the quantity box, in the cart and at checkout alike."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1491
msgid "Leave it clear to ignore them. The figures are still imported, so turning this on takes effect immediately rather than after the next product sync. Order screens and refunds are never restricted by it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1494
msgid "Both figures are shown on each product's Inventory tab, where they are read-only: Kontor supplies them and every sync rewrites them, so they are changed in the ERP."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1499
msgid "Articles without stock records"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1517
msgid "Draft imported products the stock feed does not carry"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1520
msgid "Kontor's stock list is narrower than its catalogue: it holds no record at all for some articles the catalogue lists. Left clear, those products keep the level they last had and stay published, and whether Kontor still sells an article is left to the product sync to answer."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1523
msgid "Ticking this hides a large part of the catalogue."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1524
msgid "On the account this was built against the catalogue lists 4386 articles and the stock feed carries 2945, so the first run after ticking it drafts some 1400 products. Each one comes back by itself as soon as a stock level for it arrives again."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1527
msgid "Clearing it again republishes what it drafted, on the next stock sync — unless the product sync is holding the product back for its own reason."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1533
msgid "Product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1535
msgid "Both rows are added to the product meta block, beside the article number and the categories, and each is shown only on a product that has the figure."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1539
msgid "Recommended retail price"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1557
msgid "Show the recommended retail price on the product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1560
#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1593
msgid "Label"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1571
msgid "Kontor supplies this figure on a wholesale shop only, where it sells at Ek and the UVP beside it is the price a business buying here can resell at. It is imported as _wksync_msrp and, until now, nothing rendered it."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1574
msgid "The label is shown in front of the amount. Leave it empty for the default wording in the shop's language, and remember that it is what the customer reads: the figure is stated raw, not as a saving, and Kontor lists a retail price no higher than the shop's own for a small number of articles."
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1579
msgid "EAN"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1590
msgid "Show the EAN on the product page"
msgstr ""

#: includes/Admin/Settings.php:1604
msgid "The EAN Kontor sends as Artean, held in WooCommerce's own GTIN field. EANs repeat across articles in the feed and WooCommerce refuses a duplicate, so a product whose EAN another already holds has none and shows no row."
msgstr ""

